    {
      "id": 30,
      "code": "G",
      "title": "Past continuous",
      "rule": "Past continuous *was/were + feʼl + -ing* bilan yasaladi. U oʻtgan zamonda maʼlum bir paytda davom etayotgan ishni bildiradi: *At eight I was eating dinner.* — Soat sakkizda men ovqat yeyayotgan edim. *I, he, she, it* bilan *was*, *you, we, they* bilan *were*: *They were playing football.* Inkor: *wasn't / weren't + -ing*; savol: *Was she sleeping? — Yes, she was.* *While* (…ayotganda) bilan ikki ishni birga aytamiz: *While I was cooking, Tom was sleeping.*",
      "examples": [
        "I was sleeping at ten o'clock.",
        "Dilnoza was reading a book.",
        "They were playing football.",
        "Was Bekzod watching TV?",
        "We weren't working yesterday morning.",
        "While I was cooking, Tom was sleeping."
      ],
      "words": [
